# Flash Order Automation – Setup Guide

## What it does
1. You upload client PO PDFs (MTN, Telkom, etc.)
2. The app checks your stock-on-hand report to see what you already have
3. It calculates the shortfall (what needs to be ordered)
4. It pre-fills the network order templates with the correct quantities
5. You review, adjust if needed, then download the completed templates ready to email

---

## One-time setup

### Prerequisites
- Python 3.10 or newer: https://www.python.org/downloads/
- (Tick "Add Python to PATH" during install)

### Install dependencies
Open a terminal (Command Prompt or PowerShell) in the folder containing `app.py` and run:

```
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

## Running the app

In the same folder, run:

```
streamlit run app.py
```

Your browser will open automatically at `http://localhost:8501`.

To stop the app, press **Ctrl+C** in the terminal.

---

## Using the app

### Step 1 – Upload files (left sidebar)
- **SOH Report** – the VVS stock-on-hand Excel file (`VVS - SOH Report *.xlsx`)
- **MTN Order Template** – the Flash Logical Catalogue `.xlsm` file
- **Telkom Order Template** – the Airtime Order Form `.xlsx` file
- **Client PO PDFs** – one or more VPS purchase order PDFs (MTN, Telkom, etc.)

The app auto-detects the network from the filename. You can override it if needed.

### Step 2 – Analyse
Click **Analyse Orders**. The app:
- Extracts every line item from the PDFs
- Looks up each product in the SOH report
- Calculates the shortfall
- Finds the matching row in each network's order template

### Tab 1 – Stock Analysis
Shows the full results table.
- 🟢 **Green rows** – shortfall > 0 (needs ordering)
- 🟡 **Yellow rows** – low confidence match (< 70%) – worth checking manually

### Tab 2 – Review & Adjust
Shows only rows that have a shortfall or low confidence. You can:
- Edit the **Order Qty** directly in the table
- Fix any wrong product matches
- Click **Save changes** when done

### Tab 3 – Download Templates
- Per-network summary of what will be ordered
- **Download** buttons for each completed order template
- Email draft text ready to paste
- CSV export of the full analysis

---

## Confidence scores
| Score | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| 80–100 | High confidence – match is almost certainly correct |
| 70–79 | Good – worth a quick glance |
| 55–69 | Low – review recommended before sending |
| < 55 | Very low – manually assign the correct product in Tab 2 |

---

## Tips
- Keep the SOH report, MTN template, and Telkom template in a shared folder so the team always uses the latest versions
- The downloaded templates are full copies of the originals with only the QTY column filled in – all formulas and formatting are preserved
- If a product shows "No match" in the template column, find it manually in Tab 2 and enter the quantity directly in the template before sending
